course: dictionary
lesson: 10924
title: One word, many meanings: volume
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Volume is one of them. To find the right meaning, look at the words around it. «Turn the volume down» is about sound, but «A liquid has a fixed volume but takes the shape of its container» is about space.
explain: The clues tell you which meaning to use. In «A liquid has a fixed volume», the sentence is about how much room something takes up, so volume means the space it fills. In «turn the volume up», the same word means how loud a sound is.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If «turn the amount of space up» makes no sense, then volume must mean loudness there. Do this check every time a word could mean more than one thing.
fact: Volume has four main meanings: how loud a sound is, how much space something takes up, an amount of something, and one book in a set.
fact: For a cuboid, volume = length × width × height, measured in cubic centimetres (cm³) or cubic metres (m³).
fact: In science, the volume of a liquid is measured in millilitres (ml) or litres (l), often with a measuring cylinder.
fact: Useful phrases: full volume, volume control, the volume of traffic, volume 3 of a series.
exercise: «Turn the volume down, please, the baby is sleeping.» What does volume mean here? | One book in a set | A large amount of something | *How loud a sound is | How much space something takes up
exercise: «A liquid has a fixed volume but takes the shape of its container.» What does volume mean here? | One book in a set | The amount of traffic on a road | *How much space the liquid takes up | How loud the liquid is
exercise: A box is 4 cm long, 3 cm wide and 2 cm high. What is its volume? | 9 cm³ | 48 cm³ | 14 cm³ | *24 cm³
test: «The volume of traffic on the motorway was huge at rush hour.» What does volume mean here? | The space the road takes up | A loud noise from the cars | One book about roads | *A large amount of traffic
test: Ruby borrowed volume 3 of the series from the library. What does volume mean? | How loud the library was | How much space the shelf takes | *One book in a set | The amount of books in the library
exam: «The General Sherman tree in California is the biggest single tree by volume.» Why is volume the right word here? | *It measures how much space the tree takes up | It tells how loud the tree is | It tells how many children can climb it | It tells how many books are about trees
